            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0191" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/472: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-13T17:00:00-03:00">October 13, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1484. Department’s 918, October 8, 9 p.m. As Aranha pointed out in his reply to
                    the Department’s proposal with regard to the formation of a Brazilian oil pool
                    committee (my despatch No. 5571 [<hi rendition="#italic">5471</hi>], of
                    September 29<anchor n="14" xml:id="d206-f1"/>) the Brazilian Government feels
                    that it already has such an official agency in the form of the National
                    Petroleum Council. As matters now stand, the National Petroleum Council and the
                    pool committee are working together harmoniously and I shall not press the
                    matter further unless the Department so desires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
